{"h":3106,"w":2400,"lines":[{"t":"Test 3","h":0.016280551917769448,"x":0.14842954640500258,"c":1,"y":0.066714375068391951,"w":0.058404064178466775},{"x":0.14833643569551611,"w":0.29726445515950517,"h":0.018310874796497068,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","y":0.1158195595128847,"c":1},{"h":0.025523264946971325,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading","y":0.15361882612861388,"x":0.14829100203586318,"c":1,"w":0.78609334309895829},{"h":0.018871578798705602,"t":"Passage 3 below.","c":1,"x":0.14630681903264947,"w":0.16225109100341795,"y":0.17280653450713135},{"w":0.6545130920410156,"c":1,"h":0.02633266608636764,"t":"Whatever happened to the Harappan Civilisation?","y":0.21207322401004625,"x":0.22160881077542949},{"t":"New research sheds light on the disappearance of an ancient society","w":0.62255157470703126,"x":0.23289993212870153,"y":0.25325522081182816,"h":0.022102166818789515,"c":1},{"x":0.14285714324119014,"w":0.016917292277018242,"h":0.014534883321060788,"c":1,"y":0.28924418610109748,"t":"A"},{"w":0.71090560913085943,"h":0.024463824280138824,"t":"The Harappan Civilisation of ancient Pakistan and India flourished 5,000 years","x":0.18214862698440432,"y":0.28878414612565739,"c":1},{"y":0.30931881435450026,"c":1,"w":0.6824432881673177,"x":0.18790514942897688,"h":0.020746382144060771,"t":"ago, but a thousand years later their cities were abandoned. The Harappan"},{"t":"Civilisation was a sophisticated Bronze Age society who built 'megacities' and","c":1,"h":0.021152611785908326,"y":0.32684797123381071,"w":0.69749659220377613,"x":0.18790191685387556},{"t":"traded internationally in luxury craft products, and yet seemed to have left almost","c":1,"x":0.18588366349885718,"y":0.34384436218463743,"w":0.72972391764322908,"h":0.025365906842508723},{"w":0.70707422892252603,"t":"no depictions of themselves. But their lack of self-imagery - at a time when the","c":1,"y":0.36326999019348571,"h":0.022013045861808633,"x":0.18782450068482384},{"w":0.72204427083333333,"t":"Egyptians were carving and painting representations of themselves all over their","x":0.18783917549814608,"h":0.021451084213109484,"y":0.38220743922896117,"c":1},{"w":0.33677782694498704,"h":0.019910146095487136,"c":1,"y":0.40052855338228022,"x":0.18406345377705005,"t":"temples - is only part of the mystery."},{"c":1,"t":"'There is plenty of archaeological evidence to tell us about the rise of the Harappan","x":0.18214981126564359,"h":0.022801054729159498,"y":0.43698105468958848,"w":0.75032892862955736},{"h":0.022245558169451618,"c":1,"w":0.71083236694335938,"x":0.18592990639705581,"t":"Civilisation, but relatively little about its fall,' explains archaeologist Dr Cameron","y":0.45542067497509797},{"w":0.68824254353841152,"t":"Petrie of the University of Cambridge. 'As populations increased, cities were","h":0.021870985847861291,"c":1,"x":0.18593177820002305,"y":0.47450641659861836},{"h":0.023241734550756177,"t":"built that had great baths, craft workshops, palaces and halls laid out in distinct","y":0.49223477045244435,"c":1,"x":0.18589573515456134,"w":0.70899546305338534},{"w":0.69016225179036461,"y":0.51049296504873054,"t":"sectors. Houses were arranged in blocks, with wide main streets and narrow","h":0.022648997408147853,"c":1,"x":0.18405401251314724},{"c":1,"t":"alleyways, and many had their own wells and drainage systems. It was very much","w":0.73706125895182284,"x":0.18410374110447209,"y":0.52949136350833204,"h":0.021740350274984332},{"t":"a *thriving civilisation.' Then around 2100 BC, a transformation began. Streets","y":0.54548805188252236,"w":0.70719253540039062,"c":1,"h":0.027411364465088295,"x":0.18397921008508453},{"h":0.021177824896071229,"t":"went uncleaned, buildings started to be abandoned, and ritual structures fell out of","x":0.18410066105792622,"w":0.74081797281901041,"y":0.56737780077032463,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"use. After their final demise, a millennium passed before really large-scale cities","x":0.18404217934051029,"w":0.71650609334309912,"h":0.023839062594323446,"y":0.5845876163284629},{"t":"appeared once more in South Asia.","y":0.60354520702699865,"w":0.31978162129720056,"h":0.01859346390998684,"x":0.18410437096171431,"c":1},{"y":0.63934544125675219,"w":0.75037399291992191,"t":"Some have claimed that major glacier-fed rivers changed their course, dramatically","h":0.024394382297493689,"x":0.17838895564822754,"c":1},{"h":0.022592309975117408,"w":0.73714421590169277,"c":1,"x":0.18218515204369207,"y":0.65826997486170558,"t":"affecting the water supply and agriculture; or that the cities could not cope with an"},{"x":0.18025276397828133,"h":0.023481952399495132,"t":"increasing population, they exhausted their resource base, the trading economy","w":0.72028137207031251,"c":1,"y":0.67725020194051866},{"x":0.18213842478650066,"h":0.024280861279155408,"w":0.74471761067708331,"t":"broke down or they succumbed to invasion and conflict; and yet others that climate","y":0.69448883162959574,"c":1},{"h":0.021250143253795595,"c":1,"t":"change caused an environmental change that affected food and water provision.","y":0.71448536084849923,"w":0.72384928385416669,"x":0.18225280710411995},{"x":0.18215747468643276,"w":0.74278615315755214,"h":0.021665802787982136,"c":1,"y":0.73251272118535804,"t":"'It is unlikely that there was a single cause for the decline of the civilisation. But the"},{"x":0.1802835971389006,"y":0.75139353025054867,"h":0.021934253817900373,"t":"fact is, until now,, we have had little solid evidence from the area for most of the key","w":0.74657557169596356,"c":1},{"t":"elements,' said Petrie. 'A lot of the archaeological debate has really only been well-","x":0.18219630208602419,"y":0.76834854788606977,"w":0.74462682088216148,"h":0.023228443290676082,"c":1},{"t":"argued speculation.'","x":0.18233083080845114,"y":0.78779069745250774,"h":0.019034801416833114,"c":1,"w":0.18421052296956381},{"t":"A research team led by Petrie, together with Dr Ravindanath Singh of Banaras","w":0.70518239339192701,"y":0.82496463952664301,"h":0.022276417178948016,"x":0.17842017184572009,"c":1},{"t":"Hindu University in India, found early in their investigations that many of the","x":0.18026169623994281,"y":0.84158745200891638,"w":0.67895329793294279,"h":0.024471145403899497,"c":1},{"w":0.74272282918294275,"h":0.021923146244793301,"t":"archaeological sites were not where they were supposed to be, completely altering","c":1,"x":0.18032926356361259,"y":0.86271071616712192},{"x":0.1802922966104496,"h":0.022554617425509571,"t":"understanding of the way that this region was inhabited in the past. When they","w":0.70335784912109367,"y":0.87975010861703706,"c":1},{"x":0.18034681501808544,"c":1,"t":"carried out a survey of how the larger area was settled in relation to sources of","h":0.020153095395198162,"w":0.70697021484375,"y":0.89942891327848273},{"x":0.17848872107653732,"w":0.71070114135742191,"y":0.91751107029100831,"h":0.021068155420110424,"c":1,"t":"water, they found inaccuracies in the published geographic locations of ancient"},{"y":0.93482206018872038,"c":1,"x":0.17839952062112474,"t":"settlements ranging from several hundred metres to many kilometres. They realised","w":0.75221847534179676,"h":0.024640082698903165},{"c":1,"t":"68","x":0.13345864664803989,"w":0.026315789222717267,"h":0.014534883321060899,"y":0.97238372105749271}]}